1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,303
Hello and welcome to today's 'Buyer Beware' programme, where we give you some tips

2
00:00:06,303 --> 00:00:08,050
on how to spend your money wisely.

3
00:00:08,050 --> 00:00:12,830
Now, in today's show we're looking at beds for children and babies.

4
00:00:12,830 --> 00:00:15,143
Let's start by looking at baby cots,

5
00:00:15,143 --> 00:00:18,140
that's for children of up to three years old.

6
00:00:18,140 --> 00:00:22,619
We tested three different cots all in the budget price range

7
00:00:22,619 --> 00:00:27,760
and, as usual, we will feature the good points, the problems and our verdict.

8
00:00:27,760 --> 00:00:32,226
The first cot we looked at was by Baby Safe

9
00:00:32,226 --> 00:00:34,740
and it had several good points to recommend it.

10
00:00:34,740 --> 00:00:38,626
Our testers liked the fact that it had four wheels,

11
00:00:38,626 --> 00:00:40,700
so it was easy to move around.

12
00:00:40,700 --> 00:00:45,087
The only slight problems with this cot were that it had no brakes,

13
00:00:45,087 --> 00:00:47,120
but they didn't think that mattered too much.

14
00:00:47,120 --> 00:00:50,571
At first they were a bit concerned about the side bar,

15
00:00:50,571 --> 00:00:53,079
because they felt babies could trap their fingers in it,

16
00:00:53,079 --> 00:00:56,509
but our testers felt that this was unlikely to happen

17
00:00:56,509 --> 00:00:59,920
so they have given this one a verdict of 'satisfactory'.

18
00:00:59,920 --> 00:01:06,365
The next cot was by Choice Cots and this time our testers were pleased

19
00:01:06,365 --> 00:01:10,220
to find a cot which is simple to put together-unlike others we looked at.

20
00:01:10,220 --> 00:01:14,801
On the minus side, our testers did not like the fact that the side

21
00:01:14,801 --> 00:01:18,598
of the cot did not drop down, making it difficult to pick up newborn

22
00:01:18,598 --> 00:01:19,060
babies.

23
00:01:19,060 --> 00:01:23,138
However, the real problem with this cot was the space between the bars;

24
00:01:23,138 --> 00:01:27,658
our testers found they were too wide and a baby could easily trap his

25
00:01:27,658 --> 00:01:28,020
head.

26
00:01:28,020 --> 00:01:32,107
We felt this was a real safety hazard and so we have labelled this

27
00:01:32,107 --> 00:01:34,000
one dangerous, I'm afraid.

28
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:37,850
And finally better news for the Mother's Choice cot.

29
00:01:37,850 --> 00:01:42,306
This cot was slightly different in that, although the side bar did not drop

30
00:01:42,306 --> 00:01:47,524
down, the base could be raised or lowered into two different positions making it

31
00:01:47,524 --> 00:01:49,330
safe as well as convenient.

32
00:01:49,330 --> 00:01:54,524
The negatives for this one were quite minor； the only niggle everyone had was

33
00:01:54,524 --> 00:01:57,814
the fact that it has no wheels and the only other problem anyone could

34
00:01:57,814 --> 00:02:01,925
find, was that there were pictures which were simply stuck on and

35
00:02:01,925 --> 00:02:03,690
so could easily become detached.

36
00:02:03,690 --> 00:02:07,060
The makers have now promised to discontinue this practice.

37
00:02:07,060 --> 00:02:10,899
As this cot will then be safe in every way, we have made the

38
00:02:10,899 --> 00:02:12,909
Mother's Choice cot our best buy.

39
00:02:12,909 --> 00:02:15,160
Congratulations Mother's Choice!

40
00:02:15,160 --> 00:02:19,200
So, what features should you look for in a baby's cot?

41
00:02:19,200 --> 00:02:25,140
Well obviously safety is a very important factor as well as comfort and convenience.

42
00:02:25,140 --> 00:02:31,180
We recommend that, if you are buying a cot, do make sure that any metal present is not rusted

43
00:02:31,180 --> 00:02:32,770
or bent in any way.

44
00:02:32,770 --> 00:02:38,733
You should ensure your cot has only rounded or smooth edging without any sharp

45
00:02:38,733 --> 00:02:42,140
edges, this is especially important for wooden cots.

46
00:02:42,140 --> 00:02:45,150
And now on to beds for toddlers...
